[{:adr/correction "corrects ADR-2607172600's framing of the read-only boundary from permanent to current-phase, per owner instruction", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607172600-kotobase-bitcoin-ethereum-clients.edn"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607172700-bitcoin-ethereum-boundary-correction", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-17", :adr/body "# ADR-2607172700: correction — ADR-2607172600's read-only boundary is current-phase, not permanent\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-17\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n**Scope**: `90-docs/adr/2607172600-kotobase-bitcoin-ethereum-clients.edn` (correction, does not touch code)\n\n## Context\n\nADR-2607172600 (`org-bitcoin-p2p` / `org-ethereum-jsonrpc`) framed the read-only / no-key / no-signing /\nno-transaction-construction boundary as \"explicitly and permanently rejected, not a phasing decision\"\nand \"a standing safety boundary... not a scope an owner instruction needs to re-litigate case by case.\"\nThe owner corrected this framing: calling it permanent is inappropriate. The right framing is that\nsigning/wallet capability is **out of scope for the current phase** of this project, to be revisited\n**as the project progresses** — not ruled out forever.\n\n## Decision\n\nRevise ADR-2607172600's characterization of the boundary:\n\n- **Before**: \"permanently... a standing safety boundary... not a phasing decision.\"\n- **After**: out of scope for the current phase. `org-bitcoin-p2p` and `org-ethereum-jsonrpc` stay\n  read-only as already built — that implementation does not change. But the absence of signing/wallet\n  capability is a **current-stage decision**, not a permanent architectural ban. As this project\n  matures and there's real justification, a dedicated follow-up ADR can add transaction construction/\n  signing/broadcast capability, with its own explicit scope, security review, and owner sign-off at\n  that time — the same \"own dedicated ADR\" mechanism ADR-2607172600 already named, just without the\n  \"permanent\"/\"not to be re-litigated\" language around it.\n\nNo code changes accompany this correction — `org-bitcoin-p2p`/`org-ethereum-jsonrpc` remain exactly as\nshipped (read-only, no keys, no transaction methods). This ADR corrects how that current state is\n*described*, not what it *is*.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Future work extending either repo (or a sibling wallet/signing repo) toward transaction capability is\n  not blocked by this ADR family — it requires its own ADR and security review, as always for\n  security-sensitive additions in this workspace, but is not pre-emptively foreclosed.\n- `90-docs/adr/2607172600-kotobase-bitcoin-ethereum-clients.edn` itself is left as originally landed\n  (ADRs in this workspace are treated as append-only historical record — corrections land as a new,\n  linked ADR rather than silently editing accepted text, same pattern as other `:adr/correction`-tagged\n  ADRs in this history).\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607172600 (kotobase blockchain-client extension — the ADR this corrects)\n", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607172700: correction -- ADR-2607172600's read-only boundary is current-phase, not permanent", :adr/source-format "edn"}]